figdown 0.1 block
# `CLASS-EMPTY-MEANING`: the meaning FIELD is mandatory and its VALUE may be
# empty. This is the language's own absent / "" / "text" tri-state (`EMPTY-LABEL-STATE`),
# which the `class` parser had been collapsing: it tested truthiness, so an
# explicitly empty meaning was rejected as if the field were missing.
#   class x            -> line error   (pinned by 302-class-decl-errors)
#   class x ""         -> legal; NO meaning claimed, NO legend entry
#   class x "Hot path" -> legal; entry drawn
# The model records "" as "", never as an omitted key: normalizing it away
# would destroy the distinction `EMPTY-LABEL-STATE` exists to preserve. A reading agent
# concludes NO category from an empty meaning (core §12.7).
class grouped "" fill=#dbeafe stroke=#1d4ed8
class hot "Hot path" fill=#fee2e2 stroke=#dc2626
node a "A" class=grouped
node b "B" class=grouped
node c "C" class=hot
edge a -> c class=hot
